From fe530549a3205ce6f3505bb5e9f025508f8f06c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:02:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [mpegts] Take the timestamps of a frame from the PES where
 the frame starts

The parsers took the PTS of a frame from the last two PES headers at the
time of the parse. The parse of a frame can wait for the next PES: HEVC
parses a NAL unit at the next start code, the parsers do not scan the
last 3 bytes of the data, and an audio frame header can span two PES.
When a short PES, as an access unit delimiter or the parameter sets in a
PES of their own (GStreamer), came before, the frame took the PTS of the
next frame.

Each PES start now keeps the PTS and DTS of its data. A video frame takes
the timestamps of the PES where its first picture starts, and the
duration from the DTS of the PES of the next frame (else the last
duration). An audio frame takes the PTS of its PES if the frame is the
first frame that starts in that PES, else the PTS of the frame before
plus the frame duration.

At the end of the data, the last frame ends at the first PES with a PTS
after its first picture, so a PES with the parameter sets before the
picture belongs to the frame. es_pts_pointer is no longer used.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
